---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'futures', title: 'Trading futures is risky' },
  { id: 'advice', title: 'Not investment advice' },
  { id: 'analyst', title: 'The analyst can be wrong' },
  { id: 'research', title: 'Research, backtests and statistics' },
  { id: 'hypothetical', title: 'Hypothetical performance' },
  { id: 'technology', title: 'Software and connections fail' },
  { id: 'tools', title: 'Copier, brackets and limits' },
  { id: 'prop', title: 'Prop-firm accounts' },
  { id: 'demo', title: 'Demo data and this website' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Risk disclaimer"
  description="Trading futures carries substantial risk of loss. Tessera is software, not advice; its analyst, research and tools can be wrong or fail. Read this before you trade with it."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="futures">Trading futures is risky</h2>
  <p>
    Trading futures and other leveraged instruments involves substantial risk of loss and is not suitable for every
    investor. Because of leverage, a small move in price can produce a large loss, and you can lose more than you
    deposited. Only trade with money you can afford to lose. Consider your experience, objectives and finances, and seek
    independent advice if you are unsure.
  </p>

  <h2 id="advice">Not investment advice</h2>
  <p>
    Tessera is software. It is not a broker, an adviser or a commodity trading advisor, and it does not know your
    circumstances. Nothing in the app or on this site, including levels, statistics, alerts and anything the analyst
    writes, is a recommendation to buy or sell. Every decision to trade is yours.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analyst">The analyst can be wrong</h2>
  <p>
    The analyst is a language model running on your own AI subscription. It can misread a chart, a level or a number,
    rely on stale data, state something false with confidence, or draft an order that does not match what you meant. Its
    drafts are proposals: read the instrument, side, size, price and bracket before you approve one.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you give a session Full access, the analyst can place, change and close orders on your accounts without asking,
    including live accounts, and it can act faster than you can follow. Use that mode only if you accept that risk, and
    set the risk limits you want before you turn it on.
  </p>

  <h2 id="research">Research, backtests and statistics</h2>
  <p>
    Research results describe how a rule behaved on past data. They depend on the data you have, how you split it, the
    costs you assumed and how many variants you tried, and they can be distorted by overfitting, look-ahead,
    survivorship and small samples. A result that held in the past may not hold in the future. Tessera shows sample
    sizes and keeps hypotheses, measurements and interpretation apart so you can judge them; it cannot make them
    predictive.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hypothetical">Hypothetical performance</h2>
  <p>
    Hypothetical or simulated performance results have certain limitations. Unlike an actual performance record,
    simulated results do not represent actual trading. Also, since the trades have not been executed, the results may
    have under- or over-compensated for the impact, if any, of certain market factors, such as lack of liquidity.
    Simulated trading programs in general are also subject to the fact that they are designed with the benefit of
    hindsight. No representation is being made that any account will or is likely to achieve profit or losses similar to
    those shown.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same applies to paper trading: fills on a paper account are simulated and can be better than you would get in
    the market.
  </p>

  <h2 id="technology">Software and connections fail</h2>
  <p>
    Tessera is in alpha. Like any trading software it can have bugs, and it depends on your computer, your internet
    connection, your broker, the trading system, data vendors and your AI provider, any of which can be slow, wrong or
    unavailable. Orders can be delayed, rejected, partly filled or filled at a worse price than you saw, and what the
    screen shows can lag the market. Keep another way to see and manage your positions, such as your broker's own
    platform or trade desk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tools">Copier, brackets and limits</h2>
  <p>
    Copying trades to several accounts multiplies your exposure, and a follower's fill can differ from the leader's.
    Brackets, breakeven, hotkeys, alerts and risk limits only act when Tessera and your connections are working, and
    only as you configured them. They are aids, not guarantees.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prop">Prop-firm accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Evaluation and funded accounts carry the rules of the firm that provides them, such as daily loss limits, trailing
    drawdowns and restrictions on news or copying. Those rules are the firm's to enforce, and Tessera does not enforce
    them unless you set matching limits yourself. Check that your use of Tessera and of trade copying is allowed by your
    firm.
  </p>

  <h2 id="demo">Demo data and this website</h2>
  <p>
    Charts, prices, orders, fills, journal figures and research results shown on this website are demo data or
    illustrations. They are not real trading results and do not suggest any result you might achieve.
  </p>
</Legal>
